  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## The recordings\n\n- **DeadCo2021-10-19.travitz.litz.schoepsCMC64v.flac24** (recommended): source not stated; 18 songs; 188 min; rated 4/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer considers this a really good audience recording; Reviewer calls it one of the best audience recordings they've heard recently [4][6]\n- **DeadCo2021-10-19.travitz.litz.schoepsCMC64v.flac16**: source not stated; 18 songs; 188 min; rated 2.5/5 by 2 [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The taper endured cold weather while recording the show [4]\n- The taper endured freezing conditions to record the show [6]\n- Jay Lane sat in on drums in place of Bill Kreutzmann [1]\n- Jay Lane sat in on drums in place of Bill Kreutzmann [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **DeadCo2021-10-19.travitz.litz.schoepsCMC64v.flac24**: taped by Jeff Travitz; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Schoeps CMC64v's>Grace Design Lunatec V3>Sound Devices 744t [1]. Also: Schoeps CMC64v mics into Grace Design Lunatec V3 and Sound Devices 744t, recorded from the 16th row, dead front center; Edited in Sound Forge Pro 15 for fades, tracked with CDWAV, encoded to FLAC with Trader's Little Helper, tagged in Foobar2000 [1]\n- **DeadCo2021-10-19.travitz.litz.schoepsCMC64v.flac16**: taped by Jeff Travitz; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Schoeps CMC64v's>Grace Design Lunatec V3>Sound Devices 744t [2]. Also: Schoeps CMC64v mics into Grace Design Lunatec V3 and Sound Devices 744t, recorded from the 16th row, dead front center; Sound Forge Pro 15 added fades and converted to 16-bit, 44.1kHz with POW-r dither; then CDWAV, Trader's Little Helper FLAC, Foobar2000 tagging [2]",
